    "body": "**Problem:** Binary GET and POST requests to `/rest/getutxos` for the same outpoints should agree. GET finds the unspent output, but POST incorrectly reports no hit.\r\nThe POST decoder writes the body into a `DataStream` with `operator<<`, serializing it as a string and prepending a CompactSize length. It then reads the first byte of that added length as the checkmempool flag, misaligning the later request fields. Hex POST bodies use the same decoding and are affected too.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Deserialize the supplied body bytes directly. Separate commits apply the existing 15-outpoint limit during decoding before allocating the vector, and use `SpanReader` to avoid the extra copy into a `DataStream`.\r\n",
